        "scope": "Ordinary movement, footprint and squeeze rules",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COMBAT_ACTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 30409,
          "sha256": "f90d039142145fbd31c37992ebece70d7926dc4b6081e340f9a2fd9dc7237bc6",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COMBAT_ACTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "## Movement and geometry",
          "line": 154
        },
        "exactAuthority": "## Movement and geometry\n\nTrack **spent movement cost**, not distance, for ordinary turn movement. Mode cap = `(1 + number of legal Dash actions this turn) × current Speed for that mode`; remaining = max(0, cap − spent cost). Switching modes never refunds cost. Recalculate cap on Speed changes, preserving spent cost. Stand from Prone costs floor(half current Speed) and requires nonzero Speed and enough budget. Dropping Prone costs no movement.\n\nFor each foot traveled, normal/difficult/severe terrain costs 1/2/3; use strongest terrain only. Add +1 for crawling and +1 for squeezing. Crawl in difficult =3:1; crawl+squeeze in difficult =4:1. A nonhostile occupied space counts as difficult terrain. Enter a hostile creature's space only with ≥two-size difference or an express feature; never willingly end in an occupied space. Squeeze through a space one size smaller, with own attack/DEX-save disadvantage and attacks-against advantage.\n\nWalk10 through difficult spends20; switch to Fly30 leaves10. Stand with Speed30 spends15; switching to Fly30 leaves15. Two legal Dashes at Speed30 give cap90; prior expenditure still counts. Interpose/Press grant5 budget: they cannot enter a difficult 5-ft tile costing10. Their separate budgets never refill ordinary movement. Ready movement uses Speed at release; Withdraw uses half current Speed. All voluntary movement requires nonzero relevant Speed.\n\nForced movement does not use these ledgers or provoke ordinary opportunity attacks, cannot place creatures in solid matter, and stops at obstacles. Teleport does not traverse intervening terrain or spend Speed unless printed; it requires a legal destination. Speed0 alone does not block forced movement or teleport. Flight with Prone/Speed0/lost support causes Falling unless Hover or an explicit magical support exception applies; use the existing fixed Fall Marker procedure. Reaching support ends Falling.\n\nNEW grid metric: each orthogonal or diagonal neighboring tile is 5 ft; use the same metric for ordinary ranges/areas. No diagonal cut through a corner when both adjacent orthogonal sides are completely blocked. Exact templates, 3D geometry, mounts, chases, jumping, climbing/swimming procedures and currents need further source review.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "6709d737368c3c1f0b6e7fb4a94974d423d519132c768b3cbde57c588f183e26",
        "trigger": "Attempted movement/placement",
        "inputs": "Actual body, route, remaining movement, terrain, squeeze/crawl",
        "outputs": "Legal displacement and actual movement expenditure",
        "lifecycle": "No free budget reset from extra events",
        "exceptions": "Spell-specific nonpath transport uses its own source",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC4",
          "AC5"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
