      "registryPointer": "/entries/5",
      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md#resolve-a-damage-event",
        "name": "Damage event and Wounds",
        "acceptanceStatus": "current-authoritative-provisional-interface",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "basis": "Current operative integration text, reused by exact accepted cohorts; not a new claim of whole-document or canon approval.",
          "cohortEvidence": [
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 6291,
              "sha256": "8dfee7f8a9cd036df80650079b289895cae245de0d8ca17bd926798de55bce2d",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json"
            },
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 7471,
              "sha256": "5590d1b66ed59287069835ea19e9ffc3d52ea32a6166a9d0645757c7202885a9",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": "Ordinary real damage packets",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 15877,
          "sha256": "69d0e64394de58c4d86a3ec57cf282978d131a1a9c1eaa21632bb7d3b72562da",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "## Resolve a damage event",
          "line": 35
        },
        "exactAuthority": "## Resolve a damage event\n\nResolve each genuinely separate hit or damage event once. Do not split one packet to multiply Wound saves or combine separate hits merely to cross a threshold. Feature-specific prevention that acts before damage or before reaching zero resolves at its printed timing first.\n\n1. Resolve attack/save, damage and applicable defenses. The remaining nonnegative amount is **resolved damage**.\n2. Record HP, Wounds and zero-HP state before the event. Remove temporary HP first. **Post-temp damage = resolved damage minus temporary HP absorbed.** Keep this amount even when it exceeds current HP; floor the resulting current HP at zero.\n3. Check V6 Instant Death. If post-temp damage minus HP before the hit is at least maximum HP, the creature dies. For a creature already at zero, this is post-temp damage at least maximum HP. Stop: there is no Wound save, death-save failure or successful knockout from that event.\n4. Otherwise, a living creature makes one Wound save if it dropped from positive HP to zero, if **2 × post-temp damage is at least maximum HP**, or if the effect actually inflicts Maiming. Overlapping triggers still cause only one save. The post-temp threshold and one-save rule are new provisional interpretations. Maiming is an independent trigger even when temporary HP absorbs all ordinary damage; immunity to Maiming itself still applies.\n5. Make a Constitution save against **max(10, floor(post-temp damage / 2))**. Use pre-event Wounds for the -1-per-Wound penalty. Maiming with zero post-temp damage uses DC 10. A Wound gained now cannot penalize the roll that created it.\n6. A success adds no Wound. A failure that began with zero, one or two Wounds adds exactly one; failure by 5 or more also gives that Wound one Injury. A failure that began with three Wounds kills the creature instead: no fourth Wound and no Injury roll. Stop processing later living-target consequences if dead.\n7. If the creature was already at zero before this event and post-temp damage is positive, end Stable. A creature using death saves adds one failure, or two for a critical hit; three failures kill it. An ordinary creature that does not use death saves dies instead, without starting death counters. A hit from positive HP to zero does not also cause a same-packet death failure.\n8. If this event newly reduces positive HP to zero, a valid melee knockout makes the surviving creature Stable. Otherwise a character/significant NPC using death saves begins dying; an ordinary monster dies. A previously Stable creature whose temporary HP absorbed all damage remains Stable unless an independent Maiming result killed it. The Director identifies significant NPCs consistently. Knockout cannot override Instant Death or a fatal Wound save.\n\nCore's Maiming and Wound trigger rules remain subject to an actual feature's eligibility. The reference helper receives already legal events; it does not grant every attack Maiming or a damage-prevention exception.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "f4c17ae8e219c584add41839a307ccda851989f7e983f1d40b15015a35bf70a2",
        "trigger": "One genuinely separate hit/damage event",
        "inputs": "Defenses, pre-event HP/Wounds, tempHP, maxHP, Maiming, critical flag",
        "outputs": "Ordered HP/InstantDeath/Wound/death-counter result",
        "lifecycle": "Single packet processed once; source lifecycle still applies",
        "exceptions": "Qualifying Null endpoint overrides only its specified consequences",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC4",
          "AC5"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
