        },
        "scope": "Ordinary living character/significant NPC states",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 15877,
          "sha256": "69d0e64394de58c4d86a3ec57cf282978d131a1a9c1eaa21632bb7d3b72562da",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "## Zero HP and recovery",
          "line": 50
        },
        "exactAuthority": "## Zero HP and recovery\n\nA living character at zero HP is Unconscious. Core's condition already includes Incapacitated, unawareness, dropping held items and falling Prone; an adjacent hit is critical as specified there. Healing does not silently remove other independent causes of Unconscious or Prone.\n\nWhile dying, make one death save at the **start of each regular initiative turn**. Roll d20 without modifiers unless a feature specifically modifies death saves. Natural 20 restores 1 HP; natural 1 adds two failures. Other results of 10 or more add one success; 9 or less add one failure. Three successes make the creature Stable; three failures make it Dead. Extra turns and Actions add no extra death saves. Stable or Dead creatures do not roll them.\n\nRegaining positive HP or becoming Stable resets both counters. Temporary HP does not raise normal HP, end Unconscious or reset counters. Fully absorbed damage does not end Stable or add a death failure in this provisional interpretation. Independent Maiming can still cause its Wound save.\n\n**Stabilize:** an Action and DC 10 Wisdom (Medicine) check, or an Action using one healer's-kit use automatically, stabilizes a living dying creature at zero. It remains Unconscious and makes no death saves. Roll 1d4 once when it becomes Stable and record its absolute recovery time that many hours later. If still Stable then, it regains 1 HP. Damage reaching normal HP cancels that deadline and resumes dying with the appropriate failures. Rest and Stable recovery use the same elapsed clock, so four hours of recovery inside an eight-hour Watch do not cost twelve hours. A later rest does not separately replay the Stable healing event.\n\n**Dead:** ordinary healing and stabilization do not restore life. Resurrection must satisfy its own willing-soul, body, time, cost and target rules. It does not automatically remove Wounds, Corruption, debts, legal death or claims upon the body. Corpses cannot supply repeated resource triggers.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "703384b91d79a60451c53e444f3a2d6c6188da363c52b6bfccc9dcc225c0fec9",
        "trigger": "Zero HP, actual regular START, healing or stabilization",
        "inputs": "Dying/Stable/Dead, counters, HP, recovery deadline",
        "outputs": "Ordinary Unconscious; source-legal death saves, Stable recovery and reset",
        "lifecycle": "Absolute recovery clock; no extra-turn death saves",
        "exceptions": "Finite summon NullDisabled0 is a separate exact source lifecycle",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC4",
          "AC5",
          "AC6-N19 (candidate)"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
