              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": "Actual roll types",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 15877,
          "sha256": "69d0e64394de58c4d86a3ec57cf282978d131a1a9c1eaa21632bb7d3b72562da",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/CORE_RESOLUTION_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "## Rolls",
          "line": 23
        },
        "exactAuthority": "## Rolls\n\nChoose the roll type before rolling. Use the actual ability modifier, including negative values, and normal proficiency only when applicable. Existing advantage/disadvantage chooses the higher/lower of two d20s; multiple sources do not stack, and any advantage plus disadvantage cancels. Add other legal modifiers once. Fractions round down unless a rule specifies otherwise. One tile is 5 feet. Class L, S and effect M retain their definitions in the shared class rules.\n\n**Attack:** roll d20 plus the appropriate attack modifier against AC. Meeting AC hits. Natural 1 always misses; natural 20 always hits and critically doubles damage dice, not flat modifiers. Beating AC by 10 is not a critical hit. An explicit broader critical range does not stack with another; use the broadest eligible range. In this overlay, a natural result below 20 in that range must still meet AC unless the feature expressly says it always hits.\n\n**Task, skill or tool check against a fixed DC:** total at least DC+10 is Critical Success; at least DC is Success; at most DC-10 is Critical Failure; other totals below DC are Failure. Natural 20 then improves one degree and natural 1 worsens one, bounded at either end. A task printing only success/failure collapses the two upper degrees to success and two lower degrees to failure; no extra consequence is invented. A natural 20 can still fail an otherwise impossible check, and a natural 1 with sufficient modifiers can still succeed.\n\n**Saving throw:** total at least DC succeeds; otherwise it fails. Natural 1 and 20 have no generic special outcome. A printed failure by 5 or 10 compares the final total with the DC; it does not add an unprinted critical-save system. Death saves are the specific exception below.\n\n**Opposed check, new provisional tie rule:** compare final totals. Higher wins; an exact tie leaves the existing state unchanged, so the initiating creature fails to change it. Do not turn task natural shifts into hidden numeric modifiers. A maneuver explicitly printing degree outcomes must specify how those apply.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "38cc462e62f987e1a5d04da68cdd231e67b24cdaddb000387f2b8a1f879effe8",
        "trigger": "Source requires an attack, save or task check",
        "inputs": "Dice, modifiers, AC/DC, advantage/disadvantage",
        "outputs": "Actual source result; only task checks use ordinary degree shifts",
        "lifecycle": "Replace dice before consequences, no duplicate event",
        "exceptions": "Death-save natural results are expressly separate",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "all ordinary spells"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
        "runtimeImplementedByRegistry": false
      },
      "scopeLimit": "Named source scopes only; no automatic extension of information disclosure, additional actions, clock bridges, historical replay, copying or source-specific root rules."
    },
    {
      "registryPointer": "/entries/8",
      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "docs/mechanics/CLASS_PLAYTEST_RULES.md#targets,-concentration-and-control",
        "name": "Concentration and control",
        "acceptanceStatus": "current-authoritative-provisional-interface",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "basis": "Current operative integration text, reused by exact accepted cohorts; not a new claim of whole-document or canon approval.",
          "cohortEvidence": [
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 6291,
              "sha256": "8dfee7f8a9cd036df80650079b289895cae245de0d8ca17bd926798de55bce2d",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json"
