      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md#null-veil",
        "name": "Null Veil damage provenance",
        "acceptanceStatus": "current-authoritative-provisional-interface",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "basis": "Current operative integration text, reused by exact accepted cohorts; not a new claim of whole-document or canon approval.",
          "cohortEvidence": [
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 6291,
              "sha256": "8dfee7f8a9cd036df80650079b289895cae245de0d8ca17bd926798de55bce2d",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json"
            },
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 7471,
              "sha256": "5590d1b66ed59287069835ea19e9ffc3d52ea32a6166a9d0645757c7202885a9",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": "Qualifying damage roots",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 59409,
          "sha256": "de147857b37ddf3e5632b067023e5863214e4c64bcee9d7a4f1190ab59beae83",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "### Null Veil",
          "line": 71
        },
        "exactAuthority": "### Null Veil\n\n**Duration.** Persists until one listed purge succeeds. Exiting field alone does not end it.\n\n**Passive Insight.** While Veil is active and not suppressed, final passive Insight is 5. This is a setting of that passive score, not omniscience or motive detection. Suppression restores normal calculation for its duration.\n\n**Creation-time nonlethal damage flag.** At creation of each damage root, record root dealer. If that dealer is a character currently under unsuppressed Null Veil, mark the entire root `nullNonlethal=true`. Descendant delayed/ongoing packets inherit the creation-time flag; later Veil changes do not rewrite it. A distinct later activation/attack creates a new root and re-evaluates. A companion/minion has its own dealer identity. Controller Veil does not convert companion damage unless an exact ability says the controller is the damage dealer. Pure transfer/redirection keeps the original root's nullNonlethal flag. It does not create a second root or extra prevention/resource triggers. An effect that explicitly creates new reflected/retaliatory damage uses the reflector as dealer and evaluates that new root at creation. A mere transfer is not reflection.\n\nWhen a root is qualifying Null-nonlethal, use this order:\n\n1. Snapshot recipient identity/lifecycle, pre-event HP/tempHP/Wounds/death state and the root nullNonlethal flag. Resolve ordinary defenses, resistance and temp-HP absorption and calculate the ordinary post-temp damage/HP loss values; attached non-damage riders remain pending under their own triggers.\n2. If nullNonlethal is false, use the ordinary CORE/HEALING_DEATH/lifecycle procedure unchanged. If true, continue below. Objects/noncreature structures still take ordinary object damage and can be destroyed; the word nonlethal does not make objects indestructible.\n3. For any living-recipient qualifying damage packet, suppress damage-caused Instant Death and suppress the packet’s Core Wound/Maiming save entirely, including half-maximum and positive-HP Wound triggers. Therefore the packet cannot create a fatal fourth-Wound result while the recipient remains above 0 or reaches 0. Existing Wounds remain recorded.\n4. Apply normal HP loss down to minimum 0. Positive→positive: stop the Null zero-state branch; recipient keeps resulting positive HP, existing Wounds/conditions and independent riders. Positive→0 ordinary living: skip damage-caused death/death-save failures and establish Stable0 with counters reset and exactly one ordinary Stable recovery deadline, unless a source-specific zero-HP permission such as actual Undying Spellform applies as stated below.\n5. Already Dying0: qualifying damage causes no new damage failure/death and does not stabilize, clear counters or move the existing death-save schedule. Already Stable0: causes no failure/death and keeps the existing recovery deadline exactly; never reroll/extend it. If temp HP absorbs the entire normal-HP loss so HP never reaches0, no zero-state transition occurs.\n6. For nonliving/companion/projection recipients, use exactly one explicit recipientLifecycle branch below; do not infer anatomy from a name. The Null override replaces only the damage-caused lethal/destruction endpoint named by that branch. Independent duration, dismissal, concentration/source end, sacrifice/cost, Hunt finality or other non-damage expiry remains real.\n7. Would-die/death-trigger protections do not trigger or spend if their prerequisite death/fatal branch was skipped by Null. A source-specific trigger keyed only to damage reducing HP to0 without killing, such as actual Undying Spellform, still triggers. Independent non-damage riders resolve if their own trigger remains true and they do not require a Wound/death result.\n8. Direct HP payments/sacrificial costs are not damage and are never converted. New reflected/retaliatory damage that is a new root re-evaluates its own dealer; pure transfer/redirection preserves the original root flag and does not duplicate root triggers.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "0594bfde9451c5f60b36b76f6ddda9c13344f0e237c3066f44e21ac60df26b00",
        "trigger": "Creation of actual damage root",
        "inputs": "Actual dealer, current operative Veil, root/descendant identity",
        "outputs": "Recorded Null flag retained by genuine descendants",
        "lifecycle": "Later dealer Veil changes do not rewrite existing root",
        "exceptions": "Named dealer/source-specific creation checkpoints only",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC5",
          "AC6 (candidate)",
          "DE4-N25 (proposal)"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
        "runtimeImplementedByRegistry": false
      },
      "scopeLimit": "Named source scopes only; no automatic extension of information disclosure, additional actions, clock bridges, historical replay, copying or source-specific root rules."
    },
    {
      "registryPointer": "/entries/10",
      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md#recipient-lifecycles-for-qualifying-null-damage",
        "name": "Null recipient lifecycles",
        "acceptanceStatus": "current-authoritative-provisional-interface",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "basis": "Current operative integration text, reused by exact accepted cohorts; not a new claim of whole-document or canon approval.",
          "cohortEvidence": [
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 6291,
              "sha256": "8dfee7f8a9cd036df80650079b289895cae245de0d8ca17bd926798de55bce2d",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_03_RECEIPT.json"
            },
            {
              "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json",
              "bytes": 7471,
              "sha256": "5590d1b66ed59287069835ea19e9ffc3d52ea32a6166a9d0645757c7202885a9",
              "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/AC5_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_05_RECEIPT.json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": "Qualifying Null damage recipients",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md",
          "bytes": 59409,
          "sha256": "de147857b37ddf3e5632b067023e5863214e4c64bcee9d7a4f1190ab59beae83",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accelerated-review-01/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/mechanics/COSMOLOGY_EPILOGUE_RELIC_NULL_PLAYTEST.md",
          "heading": "### Recipient lifecycles for qualifying Null damage",
          "line": 90
        },
        "exactAuthority": "### Recipient lifecycles for qualifying Null damage\n\n**Ordinary living recipient.** Use orderedAlgorithm steps 3–5. Positive→positive: no packet-created Wound/Instant Death. New positive→0: Stable0 unless an exact source-specific zero permission overrides. Already Dying0: same counters/markers. Already Stable0: same recovery deadline.\n\n**Ranger Beast.** Source normally dies immediately at0. Qualifying Null damage replaces that damage-caused immediate-death transition with Null Disabled at0: Incapacitated, Speed0, no commands/actions; same animal/bond remains. Ordinary legal companion healing above0 ends Disabled. A later independent non-damage death/removal rule still works.\n\n**Finite summon, Familiar or Mirror Beast.** Source normally disappears/ends at0. Qualifying Null damage replaces only that damage-caused zero disappearance with Null Disabled at0 while its original duration/source still exists. Independent duration expiry, dismissal, concentration/source end or replacement still ends it. Legal companion healing above0 restores function; no generic repair/resummon is granted.\n\n**Mage Lich elite.** Source normally becomes destroyed bound asset at0. Qualifying Null damage leaves same elite Null Disabled at0, not destroyed; therefore Soulbound is not legal solely from this zero. Legal companion healing above0 restores it. An independent actual destruction/expiry can later create its normal destroyed state.\n\n**Wizard standard undead.** Qualifying Null damage leaves same minion Null Disabled at0 instead of damage-caused destruction. Dismissal or owner completed-LR expiry still ends it. Legal healing above0 if a real source applies may restore it.\n\n**Authored local projection.** A scene projection whose authored 0-HP rule says disperse/end uses that administrative projection endpoint even under Null; it is not a living death/Wound branch. ACT-FEAST-STEWARD instead uses its explicit Collapsed Projection rule. This classification must be printed in the actor profile, not inferred from a name.\n\n**Undying Spellform.** If qualifying damage newly reduces a Mage with actual Undying Spellform to0 without killing outright, its printed trigger occurs and its 1/LR use is spent. It overrides zero-HP Unconscious/Incapacitated permissions as reviewed: conscious, half-Speed voluntary movement, normal Action, legal spellcasting/concentration, no independent BA/Reaction. Triggering damage still causes its concentration save. If still0 at feature expiry, the reviewed expiry destabilizes/cancels Stable recovery and adds one failed death save; that later feature-expiry event is not the original Null damage packet.\n\n**Would-die protections.** A protection whose trigger requires actual death/would-die/fatal result does not trigger and spends no use when Null skips that damage-caused death branch. Do not replay it later. Separate minimum-HP prevention that resolves earlier follows its own source if actually triggered.\n\n**Actual nonliving Construct.** For an actual nonliving Construct creature with an authored HP/destruction endpoint, qualifying Null damage reducing it to0 replaces only damage-caused destruction with Null Disabled0: Incapacitated, Speed0, no Actions/Bonus Actions/Reactions/commands. Same construct identity remains; no corpse/parts/loot are generated by the zero. Only an actual repair/heal rule that expressly applies to that construct can raise it above0 and end Disabled; no generic repair is granted.\n\n**Silence Wraith only.** For ACT-SILENCE-WRAITH specifically, qualifying Null damage reducing it to0 replaces its damage-caused dispersal with Null Disabled0 (Incapacitated, Speed0, no Actions/Bonus Actions/Reactions). It has no corpse/soul/loot. The chamber’s independent correct-plate terminal may still pacify/disperse that same identity; no generic healing/repair is invented.\n\n**Local actor bindings.** ACT-TOY-SENTINEL: ordinaryNonlivingConstruct; ACT-SILENCE-WRAITH: localSpirit; ACT-ACCORD-DEVIL: localProjection; ACT-ACCORD-DEMON: localProjection; ACT-ECHO-DOPPELGANGER: localProjection; ACT-FEAST-STEWARD: explicit Collapsed Projection actor rule; ACT-NULL-WITNESS: ordinaryLiving; ACT-GLASS-MENDER-SENTINEL: localProjection.\n\n**What Null Veil does not erase.** Does not remove old Wounds/Injuries, revive Dead creatures, clear existing dying counters, rewrite death history, cure conditions, or prevent non-damage lethal costs/tracks. Newly-zero stabilization resets only its current death-save counters because becoming Stable requires that under Core. Direct HP payments/sacrificial costs are not damage and are not converted. This nonlethal override does not alter Hunt finality or Hunted Death rules for actual later deaths from other causes.\n\n",
        "authoritySha256": "5a35d5c534a1de97b651a77ab803dc89bdf723479f3620f3c886191a6cd7f565",
        "trigger": "Null-marked packet reaches actual recipient",
        "inputs": "Body type/source, actual HP/tempHP, current zero state, root",
        "outputs": "Source-scoped nonlethal endpoint without phantom death/resources",
        "lifecycle": "Same extant body; true expiry/removal continues",
        "exceptions": "Does not globally make every construct/summon living",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [
          "AC4",
          "AC5",
          "AC6 (candidate)"
        ],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users, not a claim of exhaustive reverse-dependency indexing.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "The exactAuthority and named source control; normalized fields index them and create no rules.",
        "runtimeImplementedByRegistry": false
      },
      "scopeLimit": "Named source scopes only; no automatic extension of information disclosure, additional actions, clock bridges, historical replay, copying or source-specific root rules."
