    {
      "registryPointer": "/entries/91",
      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "DE4-RNG-05",
        "name": "DE4-RNG-05",
        "acceptanceStatus": "accepted-authored-video-game-candidate",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/DE4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_07_RECEIPT.json",
          "bytes": 17445,
          "sha256": "f240bbf70d2313e3383c72b6c9d201ba01eb5b4a02c01d3ea6551afd02e2dc6a",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accepted-interface-refresh-04/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/DE4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_07_RECEIPT.json"
        },
        "scope": "Only source relationships expressly covered by this exact DE4 authority; no global extension, automatic acquisition or cosmological settlement.",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/data/public/spell_candidates/divination_enchantment_rank4_reviewed_07.json",
          "bytes": 667131,
          "sha256": "5b97ea8a3e00c0e5323fb86f540feda292ad60043a1241e9baecc1eb78f0517a",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accepted-interface-refresh-04/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/data/public/spell_candidates/divination_enchantment_rank4_reviewed_07.json",
          "pointer": "/sharedRules/DE4-RNG-05"
        },
        "exactAuthority": "NEW DE4-RNG-05 proposal under the owner's video-game-only directive. Authored dice are engine RNG operations, not physical tabletop objects. The actual conjured Fate Coin remains its existing physical game-world item with the same body, custody, hand, HP, duration and consumption. A roll event has an immutable original-event ID, replacement-lineage ID, actual generating entity/local event, original source, stable ordered component IDs, original modifiers/advantage state, target set and source-defined visibility grants. Finish the complete original RNG operation before any of these reroll permissions can commit; commit before its consequences. Fate Coin selects exactly one component of the complete eligible original operation and draws the same die type once; recompute its original reduction/selection with every other component unchanged. Mark Omen and Fate Reversal replace their own complete eligible d20 procedure. These distinctions survive digital implementation.\n\nAn engine's knowledge, logging, debug access, animation, a player's camera, knowledge of the seed, or prediction of a hidden outcome grants no character/player permission. The entire original die-result set must already be available to the acting player under the original event's established gameplay-information policy, and the source's actual perception, range, line-of-effect and resource predicates must independently pass. No eligible prompt, selectable event identifier or failure reason may reveal an otherwise hidden event. If the original source has no established visibility grant, these spells grant none; a source-specific presentation decision must be authored separately. A visible summed total alone does not reveal otherwise hidden component faces or grant a one-component choice. A fixed or automatic result with no actual RNG operation supplies no reroll event. Source-defined finite uniform 1dN random draws are eligible for Fate Coin only when their original result set is already available and the other source predicates pass; an empty set creates no draw, and the previously snapshotted candidate set never changes on replacement. Arbitrary simulation RNG, generation seeds and unexposed loot/world generation are not made eligible merely by existing in engine memory. No additional replacement RNG is consumed for a rejected preflight or a paid-but-blocked alteration; record the committed cost and guard separately from whether a new draw occurred.\n\nSerialize legal commitments through the actual gameplay event queue. Simultaneous candidates use current initiative order; ties use stable preexisting actor ID then stable source/application ID. Outside initiative use those stable actor/source IDs fixed before this original event was generated. Network arrival, frame rate, client/UI order, reopening a prompt and a new replacement ID cannot change priority or create a new original lineage. A rejected later candidate spends no Reaction, token or permission. This is a scoped deterministic tie-break for these three spell permissions, not a rewrite of all interrupt priority or any class-specific reroll. Snapshot the original modifiers, including any eligible Alignment Nexus benefit, when the original roll is created; replacement retains those modifiers even if later alignment/ward changes would alter a genuinely new event. Apply only the final original event's consequences once. No additional cast, attack, target rescan, payment, hit, Wound, death event or resource grant is generated by a replacement.\n\nSOURCE POLICY BINDING: DE4-PRESENTATION-06 in this same pending revision supplies only its five explicitly proposed entries. Unlisted events remain denied. Both documents require exact joint acceptance before live application.",
        "authoritySha256": "2ef5463336c0742ac4b82c87935c9fc9ee654668bda5d4edc4ae4658badad1de",
        "trigger": "Use the exact source-specific activation and checkpoints.",
        "inputs": "Actual class/access, information, resource, geometry and lifecycle predicates in the accepted complete model.",
        "outputs": "Only the source-specific results in exactAuthority.",
        "lifecycle": "Unchanged accepted deadlines, identity and cleanup rules.",
        "exceptions": "Complete accepted model and named external interfaces control; previous versions remain historical.",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users only; shared-rule scope must be read, never assumed globally.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "Exact authority and complete source control; labels create no rules.",
