    {
      "registryPointer": "/entries/92",
      "completeEntryUnchanged": {
        "id": "DE4-PRESENTATION-06",
        "name": "DE4-PRESENTATION-06",
        "acceptanceStatus": "accepted-authored-video-game-candidate",
        "acceptanceBasis": {
          "path": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/DE4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_07_RECEIPT.json",
          "bytes": 17445,
          "sha256": "f240bbf70d2313e3383c72b6c9d201ba01eb5b4a02c01d3ea6551afd02e2dc6a",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accepted-interface-refresh-04/sources/docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/DE4_EXACT_ACCEPTANCE_07_RECEIPT.json"
        },
        "scope": "Only source relationships expressly covered by this exact DE4 authority; no global extension, automatic acquisition or cosmological settlement.",
        "currentAuthoritativeSource": {
          "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/data/public/spell_candidates/divination_enchantment_rank4_reviewed_07.json",
          "bytes": 667131,
          "sha256": "5b97ea8a3e00c0e5323fb86f540feda292ad60043a1241e9baecc1eb78f0517a",
          "frozenCopy": "docs/audit/2026-10-08/full-game/accepted-interface-refresh-04/sources/DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/data/public/spell_candidates/divination_enchantment_rank4_reviewed_07.json",
          "pointer": "/sharedRules/DE4-PRESENTATION-06"
        },
        "exactAuthority": "NEW DE4-PRESENTATION-06 — proposed narrow digital presentation policy for this conference; NOT an already accepted visibility grant. This policy grants only the following event-result presentations. It does not disclose hidden creatures, secret events, source/rank/DC/AC information, hidden modifier reasons, RNG seeds or future draws. An explicit source prohibition on disclosure takes precedence. Unlisted or unclassified events remain unavailable to these three Fate permissions until separately authored; absence of a secrecy tag is not a grant.\n\n1. OVERT-ATTACK: for an actual ordinary Core attack whose generating creature, declared attack and target are already perceived/identified by the reacting creature through its real senses, give that creature's authorized controller the complete resolved original attack d20 set before hit/miss consequences. This is an explicit new result-presentation decision, not a new sensing ability. Display the faces and which original selection rule is being applied, not the hidden causes of advantage, the target's AC or hidden modifiers. A hidden attacker or an unperceived/unknown target does not qualify under this entry. An extra camera, spectator role, battle log or engine access is not perception. An AI controller receives only the corresponding authorized view, not the entire engine state.\n\n2. OWN-REQUESTED-CHECK: an actually requested, nonsecret ordinary ability/skill/tool check presents its complete original d20 set privately to that actor's authorized controller. Automatic/secret sensing checks, protected inquiries and hidden contests are excluded. Another reacting character can use that player's legitimate display only when that reacting character independently satisfies its own actual source perception/range/LoE and resource predicates; this rule grants no character-to-character telepathy. In a multi-character player party, the player may control both actors; a multiplayer peer does not inherit another player's private grant.\n\n3. BURNING-HANDS-DAMAGE: once an actual reviewed Burning Hands cone is manifested and the shared 3d6 operation is generated, present the complete shared faces before damage consequences to the caster's controller and to controllers of reacting characters who actually perceive the caster and the manifested cone. This whitelist entry is specifically for the reviewed Burning Hands damage operation, not every damage pool. It reveals no target list, save result, resistance or hidden recipient. Per-recipient damage is still computed once from the one final shared total. A reaction holder must additionally pass its own actual Coin range/LoE/hand/custody predicates. A source-suppressed operation that creates no actual damage draw gives nothing to reroll.\n\n4. CONFUSION-BEHAVIOR: for this pending Confusion procedure, show the actual finite d4 behavior, any genuinely generated d8 direction, and any genuinely generated uniform 1dN perceived-target selection privately to the affected body's authorized controller before that behavior executes. Do not expose candidates that this body cannot actually perceive. Other controllers receive no raw selection results under this entry. A player who also controls a reacting holder can use that legitimate result view only if the reacting holder independently perceives the true roll-generating body and passes Coin's other source requirements. The snapshotted set and candidate order are immutable; an empty set makes no draw. A private NPC-controller view is not disclosed to human players.\n\n5. RESONANCE-WELL-RESERVE: show the actual initial 1d4 reserve-creation draw privately to the Well creator's authorized controller before the reserve is established. This preserves the existing timing boundary but authors its digital display; it does not expose any already-established or hidden reserve and does not permit a later reroll/refill. The reacting holder still needs Coin's real event perception/range/LoE/custody/Reaction.\n\nFor these entries only, record policyId, entryId, original event ID, the authorized controller set and the actual perception evidence at generation. Recheck the reacting source's own spatial/resource predicates at commitment. Already lawfully learned original faces are not erased by a later effect, but event knowledge alone never satisfies a currently missing character predicate. Present only information this whitelist actually grants, whether or not any observer possesses a Fate source; resource possession cannot become a detector. Total-only or hidden-result policies remain insufficient. Preserve the original RNG component IDs and reduction rule through replacement. No rejected declaration or paid-but-blocked alteration generates a replacement draw.\n\nThis is a minimum concrete policy, not a universal dice-visibility policy. In particular, unlisted enemy saving throws, trauma, secret checks, loot/world generation and private source operations remain unavailable. Future presentation entries require explicit source-specific authorship and separate review. Composition vectors that declare a visibility grant remain composition vectors; that declaration is not evidence that an unlisted live source supplies one.\n\nNEW BURNING-HANDS EVENT-EXISTENCE COMPLETION FOR CONCURRENCE: For this source only, each actually manifested Burning Hands cone generates exactly one complete original shared3d6 operation at its ordinary damage-resolution checkpoint whether the eligible recipient set is empty, entirely hidden, or includes known recipients. It is the same cast operation, not an extra roll, attack or damage packet per recipient. A cast interrupted or prevented before manifestation generates none. A manifested empty cone deals no damage and triggers no hit/damage/Wound/kill/resource consequence, even though its finite original pool is available under BURNING-HANDS-DAMAGE. Thus the presence, number, values, availability and timing of the published pool do not encode whether hidden recipients exist. No target list, saves, defenses or damage outcome is added to this presentation. A paid Coin may alter that original empty-cone pool only through its ordinary actual predicates, with its normal consumed item/Reaction/guard and no refunded cost; it creates no recipient or successful damage event. This is explicit NEW per-source RNG-generation authorship, not a rule for other empty areas or unlisted spells.",
        "authoritySha256": "ec74f56e24f2259b3a33383b07f3cfa4c5f2d37910199af9418cdfca558b4c65",
        "trigger": "Use the exact source-specific activation and checkpoints.",
        "inputs": "Actual class/access, information, resource, geometry and lifecycle predicates in the accepted complete model.",
        "outputs": "Only the source-specific results in exactAuthority.",
        "lifecycle": "Unchanged accepted deadlines, identity and cleanup rules.",
        "exceptions": "Complete accepted model and named external interfaces control; previous versions remain historical.",
        "knownSourceSpecificExtensions": [],
        "usedBy": [],
        "usageCoverage": "Explicit known users only; shared-rule scope must be read, never assumed globally.",
        "reusableWithinScope": true,
        "summaryAuthority": "Exact authority and complete source control; labels create no rules.",
