        "sourceRecordSha256": "8bb030a8bce9afd5744dc428f395603cb69d39eb91017007bbe276eff65a160b",
        "procedure": "Keep both actual placements separate. Conjuration rank 4, base 7 RP, range 60 feet: NEW Action, V/S/F creates a fixed 15-foot-radius sphere at a perceived point with line of effect, with concentration up to one minute. Snapshot each creature’s defined effective axes when it first occupies the area with line of effect to the center, including eligible occupants at creation. While eligible inside, those axes use Alignment Lock’s proposed prevention and underlying-history rules. No save or entry bar applies. Leaving removes the constraint immediately; reentry reuses that application’s first snapshot. Store priority when the application first qualifies on that creature/axis. Exit or suppression makes it inactive for priority selection without changing the original timestamp on resumption. Abjuration rank 7, base 17 RP, range 120 feet, currently Cleric: NEW Action, V/S/F targets one perceived creature with line of effect for a CHA save; a willing target can elect failure. Failure applies the effective-axis lock for seven elapsed days without concentration. Preserve cannot act against it as a bounded conduct restriction: only deliberate conduct explicitly incompatible with the locked record under an already established source predicate can be vetoed. A player chooses another legal action without spending the rejected choice’s costs; no beliefs, self-harm, confession, allegiance or new moral standard is compelled. Without an established incompatibility predicate, the clause has no invented test. A veto that would leave no legal ordinary Action or deny the whole turn additionally requires and spends the shared hard-denial allowance; after it is spent, such a whole-Action/turn veto cannot recur that encounter. The axis lock and independently legal narrower restriction continue. This NEW limiting interpretation is a proposal beside the broader original, not recovered doctrine. Neither placement grants the other’s mode, rank, price or class access.\n\nCURRENT INTERFACE — NEW scoped exception `AC4-ALIGN-01` for Alignment Lock/Alignment Anchor versus reviewed Alignment Purge/Suggestion. A Lock/Anchor application freezes only the effective defined axis value it actually snapshots; it does not delete, prevent creation of, pause, refund, or rewrite an underlying Alignment Suggestion, Alignment Purge, or independent lawful alignment record. For effective-alignment reads on a locked axis, evaluate the ordinary underlying history and reviewed Suggestion/Purge interaction (including AP-AS-01) first, then apply the active Lock/Anchor snapshot last. Thus a Purge or Suggestion cast after a lock can establish its own live record and pay/keep its own costs and clock, but cannot change the locked effective axis while that lock remains active. When a new Suggestion computes its target baseline, exclude prior Suggestion overlays and Purge overlays as AP-AS-01 already requires, and additionally exclude AC4 Lock/Anchor overlays on the target so the lock cannot become a ratchet staircase. A Purge on the Suggestion caster still affects that caster's own effective orientation normally. If Lock/Anchor is applied while Purge or Suggestion is already effective, it snapshots the currently effective defined value; later ending/suppression of the lower overlay does not alter that snapshot. When Lock/Anchor ends or is inactive because a zone was exited/suppressed, the then-live lower lawful result becomes effective immediately with its original deadline/history; no old snapshot is restored and no missed application replays. Undefined axes are never fabricated.",
        "newChoices": "NEW: two placement-specific procedures, explicit zone snapshot/priority handling, and conduct restrictions using existing predicates and shared control history.",
        "historicalWorkedCases": [
          "The Cleric placement remains rank 7 and base 17 RP. A Druid’s rank-4 zone does not lower that price or grant its own seven-day single-target mode.",
          "A Director cannot invent a moral requirement forcing a player to attack an ally. No established incompatibility predicate means no conduct veto."
        ],
        "examplesAreRuntimeTests": false
      },
      "completeSharedRules": {
        "castingEngine": "Use SPELL_INTEGRATION_RULES.md exactly: legal action/components/target/repertoire first; class-specific rank/cost; pre-cast Dissonance; commit RP/materials/concentration; apply Dissonance/Refrain/cast-begin hooks; resolve interruption; then effect. Failed/countered/saved casts refund nothing.",
        "timing": "One-minute concentration effects use the source's normal ten future caster regular-start markers in initiative or 60 elapsed seconds outside unless this card states a different exact clock. Ten minutes = 100 future caster regular-start markers or 600 elapsed seconds. Alignment Lock uses 24 elapsed hours; rank-7 Alignment Anchor uses seven elapsed days; Bind Element uses two future target regular ends / 12 elapsed seconds outside initiative. Preserve virtual/absolute deadlines through initiative changes, absence and suppression.\nSPELL SHIELD EXACT CLOCK — Because Spell Shield is nonconcentration, its own one-minute deadline is explicit: in initiative, application records the caster's tenth future regular-start marker after application, excluding any start already in progress or past. Outside initiative, deadline = application timestamp + 60 elapsed seconds. Preserve that fixed virtual/absolute deadline across initiative entry/exit, reorder, extra turns, absence, caster death and suppression. Caster death alone does not end Spell Shield.",
        "null": "Creation-time Null root identity remains governed by accepted EPI-08–14. Pure transfer/redirection preserves the root flag. New reflected/retaliatory damage only uses a new root when an exact effect says it creates new damage. Finite summons reduced to 0 by qualifying Null damage use the accepted Disabled branch while independent expiry/concentration/replacement remains real.",
        "faction": "Use standing-v1 separately from membership and invocation permission. Faction Seal's reviewed invocation-permission procedure is the permission reference where invoked. Positive standing never creates membership or permission.",
        "alignment": "Reviewed Alignment Purge AP-AS-01 remains exactly source-specific. AC4-ALIGN-01 is an additional NEW scoped exception only for Alignment Lock/Alignment Anchor; it creates no universal alignment priority engine.",
        "banishment": "Banishment is not one of these fifteen. The earlier pre-push sequencing hold is historical. Its exact source receipt is preserved and it remains the next separate procedure-authoring obligation using current planes/souls sources.",
        "summonTargeting": "NEW scoped AC4-SUMMON-TARGET-01: solely for the two authored AC4 temporary profiles Summon Water Pet and Faction Envoy, while their finite body exists they count as an active creature and as a living ally for ordinary HP-healing/living-creature targeting, including Cleric Healing Rite. This is a mechanical targeting classification only; it establishes no natural origin, biology, soul, corpse, loot, undead/construct taxonomy or cosmological identity. Null Disabled 0 remains the same existing body and may receive an otherwise legal heal; an ended/expired/dismissed body is no longer a target. Resonance Beacon uses active-creature identity rather than biological 'living' status: an enrolled creature must still be able to spend its own Action and RP."
