          "originalQuestion": "Preserve copying ONE NON-DAMAGING SPELL CAST IN THE LAST3ROUNDS,Core Action/120ft/Instantaneous. Define the historical eligibility window,caster observation/knowledge,legal source spell rank/access and non-damaging classification including indirect summons or delayed harm. Compare Cast Echo,whose source permits any spell; preserve this narrower qualifier without merging identities. Decide new casting costs/components,Action and concentration,targets/range,save/DC and copied choices. Copying a spell is not replaying a past outcome,duplicating an already-spent item or learning a spell permanently. Prevent recursive copies of copies and revived one-shot effects through explicit source-event lineage,not by silently removing the printed copy capability.",
