          "completeProcedure": "KEEP one non-damaging historic spell copy, Action/V/S/F/base 17 RP and the source three-round window. NEW select exactly one actual original spell-cast event that the echoer directly perceived and identified when cast, with original casting completed no more than 18 elapsed seconds before Fate Echo commitment, inclusive at 18. Record its original caster, event/cast ID, exact source version, original generating class/mode/school/rank, completed-casting timestamp and real observation/line-of-effect receipt within 120 feet then. The original caster need not still be present. The event must already have survived interruption and successfully reached its own effect resolution; no countered attempt, rumor, item activation, nonspell technique, false image or merely recognized later residue qualifies. For a readied original, preparation is its casting timestamp; later release supplies neither a fresher cast nor a second cast. A still-unresolved held original is ineligible.\n\nNEW finite mode gate: its complete authorized operative mode has actual rank 0 through 7 and normal casting time one Action or Bonus Action. A null rank is not 0; a Reaction or longer-casting mode is not admitted. Use the exact observed mode, generating school/rank and source version, not a donor's lower alternative placement or a fabricated nondamaging subset. Original optional metamagic, item modifications, borrowed casting resources or donor stats are not copied as free benefits. A genuinely distinct complete nondamaging mode may qualify, but a damaging mode that missed does not. Reject any mode that itself supplies immediate, delayed, periodic or conditional damage, direct HP loss, lethal assignment, a damaging body/summon/trap, damage rider or granted damaging attack. Later independent voluntary acts do not automatically make ordinary protection/information/healing/control damaging. Reject copying/echo/release/contingency/further-casting-access mechanisms and every copy-descended event, including Fate Echo itself. Actual no-copy restrictions and independently required grants remain.\n\nNEW temporary copied-spell route: Fate Echo waives only the ordinary learned/prepared/class-list permission for this single admitted payload. It does not acquire a class feature, feat charge, artifact permission, source-specific stock, independent per-rest entitlement, permanent repertoire or new pool. The echoer must satisfy all nonwaived payload predicates, actual independent uses/costs, targets/consent, equipment, body, environment and other required source engines. An intrinsic identity-wide limited-use ledger remains the same ledger across real routes; this permission never resets a spent allowance. Where the copied source itself supplies a universal per-user limit, first actual use records that source's normal first-use allowance, not a second acquired class/feat grant. Where a separate acquired engine grants a charge, that charge must actually exist. If an indispensable operand/credential has no actual source or explicit adapter below, that particular payload is inadmissible, not partly invented or silently stripped. Cast Echo, Mirrorsage Echo Release and feat copies keep their own separate unadopted/reviewed scopes.\n\nNEW two-stage paid composite: at declaration fix the copied event/mode and fresh legal target choices (Ready exception below), validate the complete forecast transaction in chronological order, and exclusively reserve its real nested RP/material/use obligations. Quote outer Fate Echo from the current state, then simulate its exact mandatory strain/history and known mandatory beginning changes to determine whether the child could legally start and pay. Do not quote both from the same old Dissonance. If a known inevitable outer transition would block or make the child unaffordable, reject the composite before spending. Reservation is not payment and cannot be spent by a competing declaration. Commit only the outer Action, its actual price/components, concentration transition and ordinary cast-start history/hooks; then open its normal Counterspell window. If it is negated, no child begins: release only unspent child reservations, keep every actual outer payment/history, and create no child cast/strain/concentration change.\n\nOn successful outer resolution, immediately revalidate the child against the actual intervening state, including any genuine Reaction cast, current legal targets/materials, resource availability, strain block and selected original mode. Reprice from that actual state. A higher actual child quote requires real unreserved funds as well; insufficient funds or another now-failed predicate ends the copy opportunity with outer costs kept and no child commitment. Do not reserve fictitious discounts or automatically replace a target/source. If valid, commit the child's own full actual price, components, consumed materials, independent uses, concentration and strain/history once, then open a separate normal Counterspell window for that child. No second Action or Bonus Action is charged: this is an explicit one-Action/two-cast exception, not an extra full Action grant. Countering the child retains both actual payments and child history. Resuming either parent never rewrites a later intervening cast's Refrain/history. No recursive cast or ungranted Action follows.\n\nNEW precise child adapter: the child has its observed generating school/rank and uses the actual Fate Echo provider's casting ability, the echoer's current ordinary PB, its own spell attack PB+ability/DC8+PB+ability and its own body/stats. Intrinsic explicit caster-class-level scaling substitutes the real Fate Echo-granting class level, not total level or the donor's level. It is a fate-echo-copy route, not a prepared/always-prepared Wizard matrix, ordinary learned Shaman spell, Mirrorsage Echo Release, feat charge or donor class card acquisition. Price begins with the ordinary rank table plus every actual independent source cost and applicable universal modifier; a class card's expressly replacement printed spell price is its replacement base, not that base plus the rank table. No donor price waiver or free class/feat charge is inherited. Use common spell Dissonance 0/1/2 by actual rank and normal chronological Refrain, actual Limit and legal casting blocks. Prepared-matrix first-distinct exemptions/Matrix modifications, a Shaman ordinary-spell-only totem vent and Mirrorsage release exemptions do not apply merely from the payer's class or a matching name. A genuinely broader existing modifier/paid concentration exception may apply only by its real predicate. Preserve negative restrictions as well as qualifying modifiers.\n\nKEEP the generic no-duplicate-copy-proc guard, correcting the proposal's unrestricted child cast-trigger phrase. Mandatory cast legality, costs, components, strain/history, concentration and counter windows still occur. The child grants its intrinsic lawful spell result and ordinary consequences, but generates no additional class/feat cast-proc, resource-refund, action-grant or copy chain merely because it is a second paid cast. The outer Fate Echo retains its own ordinary permitted hooks. This does not strip an otherwise legal intrinsic finite payload result; no resource loop or independent use reset is permitted. Starting a concentration child ends incompatible prior concentration at child commitment, not outer declaration, unless an actual paid linked-effect source expressly applies. If the child is later countered, displaced concentration is not restored. The child's F uses the echoer's actual permitted casting focus; an explicitly special/consumed material still requires that actual item. All child V/S and other components are performed at its own commitment, not supplied retroactively by the outer cast.\n\nTargets originate at the echoer and use the copied mode's own range/line/effect/consent rules, not an extra 120 feet. Fresh outcomes use actual rolls and current defenses, never the donor's result. Result ownership is the echoer's, with original/copy lineage, independent cast/application IDs, fixed generating rank and actual new effect deadlines retained. Acquired hard-control and source-wide quantity/recipient limits remain shared; an old consumed object/effect is not restored.\n\nNEW bounded Ready integration: generic Ready may hold this Action-time spell. Choose the qualifying original at preparation, apply the 18-second gate then, pay/cast the outer once, reserve the child and maintain the actual held-spell concentration. Select fresh legal release targets under Ready's ordinary rule. The original cannot be exchanged and its freshness is not rebased; a valid earlier preparation does not fail solely because ordinary held time elapsed. Invalid/declined release spends no Reaction or child cost and can await another valid trigger before the same Ready expiry. At a legal release spend the actual permitted Reaction once and release the outer without another outer cost/hook/counter window; relinquish the nonconcentration outer hold and perform the child's actual revalidation/commit/counter sequence there. This expressly new nested cast at release is not a second outer cast and does not grant another Reaction. An expired/interrupted hold keeps outer payments and releases only unspent child reservations. No hold, expiry, retarget or counter grants a second copy opportunity.",
          "workedCases": [
            "DI7-04-A: Conditional Wizard13 INT+4/PB5 has RP48, Dissonance0, no prior same-name Refrain and Fate Echo as its first prepared-matrix family of a genuine encounter. It directly witnessed an eligible complete rank1 nondamaging original at0; commitment at18 qualifies. Outer price17 leaves31 and its actual prepared-family exemption yields0 base strain. The child is a copied route, not another matrix: base2 leaves29 and common rank1 base strain gives Dissonance1. Both have distinct cast IDs; fresh lawful targets/components and independent uses are required. If the Fate matrix exemption was already spent, the same low-strain prices leave29 but Dissonance becomes3, not1.",
            "DI7-04-B: Reject a damaging spell that missed, a copy-descended event and a source19 seconds old. In a separate legal copy, countering the outer spends only the actually committed outer obligations and releases unused child reservations; there is no child history. If the child was committed and countered, both actual payments and both histories remain spent. A copied Reaction-only Shield mode is ineligible despite being nondamaging."
          ],
          "examplesEvidenceKind": "Authored conditional examples; no claim of full-procedure execution.",
          "summaryFieldsDoNotReplaceFullProcedure": true
        },
